      "writtenOn": "2019-02-27T02:38:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually I think my last statement was wrong; need to refresh my ARM assembly a bit.\n\n\"bl\" behaves as described, but it\u0027s intended to call a subroutine (in this case exception_panic) and then that should return to the next instruction (via the link register).\n\nThe noop/empty could be used for alignment of the data load of 0xdead6660. exception_panic is also marked \"noreturn\", so it shouldn\u0027t ever return to the noop/empty instructoin, but will look a bit more in depth tomorrow because now I\u0027m curious.",
      "parentUuid": "2714a1bc_88ba9d5d",
